L=['# Operator-first normal Green: weighted proof and cost obstruction','', '**Decision: PROOF / CONCEPT MILESTONE, not solver promotion.** A concrete inverse-action representation was constructed without the full dense Green inverse. Both fixed original-A0 tests passed. Its present factor layout loses to the existing angular-band baseline in storage, setup and probe application. No rank/tolerance sweep or outer-RTE trial followed.','', '## What changed','', 'The failed prior normal H representation compressed an already computed inverse, controlling inverse energy rather than original-operator defect. Here the known scalar Fourier differentiation matrix is compressed first, while the entire local12-angle collision matrix stays intact. A recursive Woodbury elimination factors that approximate operator directly. Its construction does not use response snapshots, teacher solutions or any full(12N)-dimensional inverse. Dense original LU is used only as a control.','', 'The invariant object is the actual layered A0(k), N128, modes k=0 and8, full g=.65 phase, actual min/gather profiles, stored rounded directions, stored normal frequencies and the complex negative Nyquist. All original-A0 residual tests retain1e-10 and max3 repairs. This is not a full heterogeneous2D solve, a learned solver, a new physical regime or a many-RHS deployment claim.','', '## Finite-dimensional proof','', 'In space-major order, G=D tensor Cn + blockdiag_j(t_j I-s_j K+i*k_t Ct). D is the Fourier derivative with actual real stored frequencies; Cn and Ct contain the actual real angular velocities. Define alpha=min_j[t_j-s_j*lambda_max((K+K*)/2)]. Its evaluated value here is '+f"{D['coercivity_alpha']:.12g}." ,'', 'For every x, Re<x,Gx> >=alpha||x||², since normal and tangent streaming are skew-Hermitian. Replace D by a skew-Hermitian Dtilde, retain local collision exactly, and call the result Gtilde. The same alpha applies, so ||Gtilde^{-1}||<=1/alpha. Consequently, in exact arithmetic,','', '    ||I-G Gtilde^{-1}|| <= max|omega_n| ||D-Dtilde|| / alpha = q.','', 'For x0=Gtilde^{-1}b and original-equation residual repairs x_{j+1}=x_j+Gtilde^{-1}(b-Gx_j), the relative residual is at most q^(j+1). This is the implication that the earlier unweighted inverse compression lacked. It applies to the actual stored-value discrete model, not an assumed continuum Green function.','', 'Construction: first Dbar=(D-D*)/2. On each binary-tree sibling pair, truncate one scalar off-diagonal SVD and set the other block to its negative adjoint. Keep dense diagonal leaves. The paired error [[0,E],[-E*,0]] has2-norm ||E||; same-level pairs are disjoint. Therefore ||D-Dtilde|| is bounded by ||D-Dbar|| plus the sum across depths of the largest per-block Frobenius truncation error. Ranks are outputs of a predeclared absolute budget alpha*1e-3/(2*max|omega_n|*4), not searched parameters.','',f"The measured derivative skew-projection discrepancy is {D['derivative']['skew_projection_error_F']:.6g}; assembled Dtilde has exactly zero measured skew defect. The hierarchy bound is {D['derivative']['hierarchy_norm_upper_bound']:.9g}. An independent sqrt(1-norm*infinity-norm) bound is tighter, {D['derivative']['row_column_norm_upper_bound']:.9g}, yielding q={analysis['model_right_defect_bound']:.9g} and q^4={analysis['model_after3_repairs_bound']:.9g}.",'', '**Proof scope:** the inequalities are analytical; alpha, SVD factors and norm bounds were evaluated in ordinary floating point, not interval arithmetic. For a computed action Bhat, E=I-Gtilde Bhat gives I-G Bhat=(I-G Gtilde^{-1})+(G Gtilde^{-1})E, so the bound becomes q+(1+q)||E||. Actual probes measure the corresponding per-input defect, not a uniform floating-machine theorem. Original residuals are still checked after every repair.','', '## Concrete no-full-inverse factor','', 'At a node, Gtilde=[[A,U_L V_R*],[U_R V_L*,B]]. Child solves construct W_L=A^{-1}U_L,W_R=B^{-1}U_R, then M_L=V_L*W_L,M_R=V_R*W_R. Factor S=I-M_L M_R. With yL=A^{-1}bL,yR=B^{-1}bR and cL=V_L*yL,cR=V_R*yR, solve a=S^{-1}(cL-M_L cR), b=cR-M_R a; output yL-W_L b and yR-W_R a. This eliminates the paired24r update through a12r Schur system. All W, M, Schur LU and pivots are counted. No extra low-rank compression occurs inside the factor.','', 'The exact child operators remain accretive and invertible; that does not guarantee benign small-Schur floating conditioning. A separate deterministic recursive algebra unit test passed with residual '+f"{D['unit']['action_residual']:.4g} and dense-solution difference {D['unit']['relative_solution_difference']:.4g}.",'', '## Fixed numerical evidence','', 'Three predetermined normalized complex random columns, one exact-zero column and one1e-200 scaled column were used per object. No physical RHS or reserved data was accessed. The same probes and original-G contract were used for all methods. Both controls and candidate preserve zero/tiny columns.','', '| k | Raw original residual, max | Raw Gtilde solve residual, max | Original residual after repair, max | Repairs |','|---|---:|---:|---:|---:|']
